      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "stereotype_of_overpreparedness",
      "label": "Stereotype of overpreparedness",
      "description": "The meme implies that the subject (T.I.) is unnecessarily cautious or overprepared, which can be interpreted as a stereotype that dismisses preparedness as irrational or excessive. This stereotype is often used to mock individuals perceived as overly cautious or 'over-the-top' in their behavior.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
